From 14087ce4ee3c741696714f5289de9bfa78bad18a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:31:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gallium/pvr: advertise GL_EXT_texture_mirror_clamp_to_edge
 (TPU FLIP_ONCE_THEN_CLAMP)

The TPU has an address mode named FLIP_ONCE_THEN_CLAMP, which is exactly GL_MIRROR_CLAMP_TO_EDGE
(mirror once past the edge, then clamp), and the sampler state already maps
PIPE_TEX_WRAP_MIRROR_CLAMP_TO_EDGE to it. The cap that advertises the GL extension was never set, so
the state tracker converted to CLAMP_TO_EDGE instead.

Set caps.texture_mirror_clamp_to_edge. The ES2 extension list grows 68 -> 69.

Verified with a new probe (tools/verify/mirror_probe.c): a 4x1 texture sampled at u = -0.4 gives
(200,0,0,255) - mirrored back into the first half - exactly the zink result; with clamping it would
have been (64,0,0,255). Full gate green: gltri 49 modes, mip 28, rttest PASS, MRT 2/4, instancing,
sRGB, border-clamp probe, 0 faults.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
index 3106ae45..0d009aee 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
@@ -293,6 +293,9 @@ pvr_screen_create(int fd, const struct pipe_screen_config *config,
       if (PVR_HAS_FEATURE(&screen->dev_info, pbe_filterable_f16))
          caps->texture_half_float_linear = true;
       caps->vertex_element_instance_divisor = true;
+      /* The TPU has FLIP_ONCE_THEN_CLAMP, which is exactly GL_MIRROR_CLAMP_TO_EDGE (mirror once past
+       * the edge, then clamp). Sampler state already maps PIPE_TEX_WRAP_MIRROR_CLAMP_TO_EDGE to it. */
+      caps->texture_mirror_clamp_to_edge = true;
       /* Multiple render targets: the PBE writes one emit per attachment (EOT program) and the
        * fragment variant maps data0..3. ES3 needs 4; v1 requires a shared format (see flush). */
       caps->max_render_targets = 4;
-- 
